problem_statement:
MaxMindDB decoder buffer bounds check inverted

#### Description

The buffer bounds check in the MaxMindDB decoder has been inverted, causing it to return an offset error when the buffer actually has sufficient data to read from.

#### Steps/Code to Reproduce

```go
package main

import (
    "fmt"
    "net"

    "github.com/oschwald/maxminddb-golang"
)

func main() {
    db, err := maxminddb.Open("GeoLite2-City.mmdb")
    if err != nil {
        panic(err)
    }
    defer db.Close()

    ip := net.ParseIP("8.8.8.8")

    var record interface{}
    err = db.Lookup(ip, &record)
    if err != nil {
        fmt.Printf("Error: %v\n", err)
        return
    }

    fmt.Printf("Record: %+v\n", record)
}
```

When running this code with a valid MaxMind database, it now fails with an offset error even though the IP lookup should succeed and return valid geolocation data.

